silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.07_preserved_material_01.concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApex is the concrete household cat Mittens, treated as the colimit apex of the household-side diagram D_Mittens whose typed legs the transport functor F must preserve. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.07_preserved_material_01.concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed silm:hasLongDescription "The FunctorialTransportNamed is the named transport functor F from the household category C to the schema category D, sending each ontology arrow to a typed schema arrow. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.07_preserved_material_01.concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_07_preserved_material_01_concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex silm:hasLongDescription "The TransportedMittensApex is the schema-side image of Mittens under F, the cocone apex through which every transported household-side leg must factor. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F(Mittens)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
